## Surfaces Delivered

### A. Generate + Run View
- Mutation: generateImsManual(input: {}) — no tenantId (SCHEMA-5)
- Typed errors: ORG_PROFILE_REQUIRED (message + link), NO_STANDARDS_IN_SCOPE, GENERATION_UNAVAILABLE
- Run view: listGenerationRuns(limit:10), section states (PROSE/GAP/NA_JUSTIFIED/FAILED/PENDING)
  - NOTE: GenerationRun.sections use UPPERCASE kinds (schema enum); this is correct
    for the run view. The document content JSON (derive.ts) uses lowercase — the
    document-viewer handles that mapping.
- Section headers: clauseRefs resolved via registryMap (passed from page.tsx) to
  display `${standard} ${clauseNo}` from the clause_registry table.
- GAP CTA: keyed off requiredSources from the registry entry matching the
  section's clauseRefs UUIDs. Links to /m5 (risk), /m3 (audit), /m2 (CAPA),
  /m4 (records), /forms (training, legal, objectives). Behavioral test asserts
  a GAP section with register.risk_assessments renders "Risk Management" link.
- Section review: markSectionReviewed(input:{sectionId}) — gated by canApprove(role,'M1')
- WebSocket: onGenerationProgress(tenantId:$tenantId) via useTenantSubscription
  - Event types: Generation.SectionComposed / SectionFailed / RunCompleted
  - Updates section states in real-time; refetches on RunCompleted
- Polling fallback: setInterval(refetchActiveRun, 10_000) while activeRun.status==='RUNNING'
  — covers subscribe race and honest degradation if WSS fails.

### WebSocket delivery observation (§3A mandate):
- Subscription wired via useTenantSubscription hook (proven pattern from m5/page.tsx).
- Enabled ONLY when activeRun.status === 'RUNNING'.
- 10s polling fallback active independently of subscription events — refetchActiveRun
  runs on interval regardless of whether onData fires.
- Architect confirmed live WSS delivery works end-to-end (positive + C-6 negative).
  The poll covers subscribe race / reconnect gaps.

### B. Document Viewer (derive.ts contract — round 2 fix)
- Content contract: `assembleManualContent` output from services/qms-generation/src/derive.ts
- frontMatter.purpose = BC-1 disclaimer text (ALWAYS rendered in .disclaimer block)
- frontMatter.normativeRefs[0].source = ISO store link (rendered as <a>)
- Sections use LOWERCASE kind: 'prose' | 'gap' | 'na_justified' | 'failed'
- clauseRefs = [{standard, clauseNo}] — rendered as `${c.standard} ${c.clauseNo}`
- prose sections: sentences[].text joined as paragraph spans
- gap sections: gap.missingSources rendered as named list items (NO sentences field)
- na_justified: naJustification string rendered with N/A label
- failed: explicit "Failed" marker (no body content in derive.ts output)
- Review state: NOT in content JSON. Joined via listGenerationRuns → find run
  where manualDocumentId === documentId → map run.sections by harmonizationKey →
  get sectionId + reviewedBy + reviewedAt per content section.
- Review action: markSectionReviewed(input:{sectionId}) — sectionId from the
  run section join, not from content. Button gated by canApprove(role,'M1')
  AND section.kind === 'prose' AND runSection exists.
- Submit for approval: submitDocumentForApproval(id)
  - UNREVIEWED_SECTIONS → t('unreviewedSections') (dedicated i18n key)
  - UNRESOLVED_GAPS → t('unresolvedGaps')
  - SoD violation → t('sodViolation')
  - Success → t('submitSuccess') visible in success banner
- CONTENT_UNAVAILABLE → graceful t('diffUnavailable') state

### C. Diff View
- getDocumentVersionDiff(v1, v2) → Diff { additions, deletions, content }
- Version picker: checkboxes on version list, compare button when 2 selected
- Content parsed: { [harmonizationKey]: { added[], removed[], kindChange? } }
- Added lines: green tint bg; removed lines: red tint + strikethrough; monospace
- CONTENT_UNAVAILABLE → "diff unavailable" state
- Single-version / empty states: first-class (no document has v2 yet)
- Retry: fetchDiff extracted to useCallback, used by both the [v1,v2] effect
  AND the ErrorState onRetry prop (no infinite spinner).

